CC BY-SA 3.0 was chosen to match the license of the Googology Wiki (Fandom),
which is where the external analyses this project checks itself against are
published, so that material can flow in both directions without a license
mismatch.

**Attribution.** If you reuse this work, credit
"koteitan, bms-rathjen (<https://github.com/koteitan/bms-rathjen>)"
and indicate whether you changed anything.

**Note for reusers of the Lean sources.** CC BY-SA is a content license, not a
software license: it has no source-provision clause, no patent grant, and is not
compatible with the GNU GPL or most other software copyleft. If you want to reuse
`lean/` inside a software project under a different license, please open an issue
— relicensing that part is a decision the maintainer can make.

