## External sources

This repository does **not** contain any of the documents below. They are read
from a local directory supplied at run time (see `scripts/external-check.py` and
`scripts/hexirp-rathjen-check.py`), and cited by URL. The source is authoritative;
a local copy is only a copy.

Licensed CC BY-SA 3.0 (Googology Wiki / Fandom):

- Hexirp, 「バシク行列システムの解析」(1–3) and 「バシク行列システムと Rathjen の
  弱マーロの psi の対応」 — <https://googology.fandom.com/ja/wiki/ユーザー:Hexirp/執筆した記事の一覧>
- P進大好きbot, 「超限変数拡張ブーフホルツのψ関数観察日記」 —
  <https://googology.fandom.com/ja/wiki/ユーザーブログ:P進大好きbot/超限変数拡張ブーフホルツのψ関数観察日記>

Other external material, cited but not included:

- M. Rathjen's papers on T(M), χ and ψ (1990, 1991, 1994) — copyrighted; cited
  bibliographically only.
- "BMS vs Rathjen's OCF" spreadsheet —
  <https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1UkVwMxbo_i9JVh9suHZF6ycp2yaIrHRZR0XZceB5BRs/edit>
- Naruyoko, googology implementations — <https://github.com/Naruyoko/googology/>.
  `lean/Trans/Recal.lean` is a **port** of `pss-vs-buchholz/common.js`; the
  function names correspond one to one (see `scripts/external-check.py`).
  `padicBotRathjen/` is used only as an external cross-check, never copied.
- yaBMS (koteitan), the C reference implementation of BMS expansion —
  <https://github.com/koteitan/yaBMS>. Used as an oracle via `scripts/crosscheck.sh`
  and `scripts/standard-audit.sh`.
